# Rendered by paisans. Do not edit: `paisans deployment apply` overwrites this file.
#
# Routing for {{ .App.Name }}, imported by the host block for
# {{ .Hostname }} in the Caddy on the monitor's own site.
# The UI, its sign in and the OAuth2 callback, and the API and realtime
# stream the UI reads pass, all of which the hub authenticates itself. The
# agents dial the hub on the mesh, never through here.
#
# Refused here: PocketBase's superuser panel, /_/ and everything under it,
# and the superuser API it signs in through, the _superusers collection and
# everything under it, auth-with-password, the OTP routes and the records
# among them. Both sign in with the superuser's password alone, and nothing
# an operator does day to day needs either from the internet. PocketBase
# finds a collection by its name or by its id (core/collection_query.go,
# FindCachedCollectionByNameOrId, at v0.40.5), and the id of _superusers is
# pbc_3142635823 on every hub, "pbc_" and the CRC-32 of "auth_superusers"
# (core/collection_model.go, idChecksum), so both are refused. They stay
# reachable over the mesh, on the hub's port {{ .App.Port }} at the
# monitor's mesh address. What passes is break glass when the identity
# provider is down, Beszel's own password sign in through the users
# collection, and everything else. Caddy's path matcher already ignores
# case, as PocketBase does a collection's name, and /_/* matches /_/ itself.
@superuser_panel path /_ /_/*
respond @superuser_panel 404
@superuser_api path /api/collections/_superusers /api/collections/_superusers/* /api/collections/pbc_3142635823 /api/collections/pbc_3142635823/*
respond @superuser_api 404
reverse_proxy{{ range .Upstreams }} {{ . }}{{ end }} {
{{- if .UpstreamElsewhere }}
	# One site, not the gateway's machine; see upstream_single in the Caddyfile.
	import upstream_single
{{- end }}
	header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
}
